## What we do
Develop and promote co-curricular programs; coordinate weekend activities and services Provide structural, networking and financial support for approved clubs and organizations (https://www.ramapo.edu/clubs/) Advise the College Programming Board Supervise operations and employees of: C (https://www.ramapo.edu/ccec/)ivic and Community Engagement Center (https://www.ramapo.edu/ccec/): Community service, non-partisan civic education, and alternative break programs CSI main office: Front desk staff and building managers Commuter Affairs: (https://www.ramapo.edu/csi/commuter-affairs/)A community where commuter students can connect to academic, social, and leadership opportunities for incoming & returning RCNJ students. Fraternity & Sorority Life (https://www.ramapo.edu/greek/): Greek system and events J. Lee’s: Lounge and game room with pool table, table tennis, Wii and Xbox 360 systems, free popcorn and events Roadrunner Central: Tickets for off campus events including Broadway shows and sporting events; discounted movie tickets Student Activities Resource Management (SARM): Club financial center Women’s Center & LGBTQ+ Services (https://www.ramapo.edu/womenscenter/): A welcoming space and caring community for people of all genders and sexualities Office of Violence Prevention: (https://www.ramapo.edu/student-affairs/ovp/) Engages the campus community in evidence-based prevention education to eliminate sexual and relationship-based violence, including dating violence, sexual assault, and stalking Ensure compliance with state and college policies Student activities are housed within the Center for Student Involvement (CSI), which falls under the Student Well-being Core. We are committed to maintaining a vibrant campus community, meeting college-wide goals, addressing the social and intellectual needs of the student body, and complementing the Ramapo College mission.
